1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,994
The water in this cloud weighs 500 tonnes.

2
00:00:03,494 --> 00:00:09,074
A puffy cloud a kilometre across holds about 0.5 g of water in each cubic metre.

3
00:00:09,574 --> 00:00:13,872
Over a billion m³, that adds up to 500 tonnes.

4
00:00:14,372 --> 00:00:20,876
It floats because the droplets are tiny, so they fall very slowly, and rising air holds them up.

5
00:00:21,376 --> 00:00:22,781
Heavy, but spread thin.
